Hi Marcus,

Thanks again for coming by today. The one-pager is attached.

On the two questions you asked:

Retention. We don't have retention numbers yet, and I don't want to make one =
up. What we'll have by mid-October: two pilot users onboarded with their real=
 data (one Berkeley PhD student, one CMU postdoc), and whether they open Enge=
lbart in week 2 without us nudging them. That's the number we're watching.

Who pays. Individual researchers first, at about $15/month. The bigger bet is=
 lab licenses, because the person who most wants provenance across a lab is t=
he advisor, not the student. We'll ask both pilot users what they'd pay and w=
ho would approve it.

I'll send a short update after the pilots.

Best,
David

